WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:00.709 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  how did the devastating death of a child  put bevis and butthead at the center of  a media firestorm the whole story is  almost too weird to believe bevis and  butthead do the universe premiered  exclusively on paramount plus but before  the audience even got a chance to see  the movie it was already shaping up to  be one of the best reviewed films of the  year critical response for beavis and  butthead do the universe has been nearly  universally positive however that's not  how critics have always felt about  beavus and butthead for instance when  the show premiered on mtv in 1993 the  critical response was mixed at best  despite critics often wringing their  hands over the series beavis and  butthead went on to become mtv's highest  rated program it was a massive hit among  kids and teens in 1993 and that  generation has now grown up to become  today's movie and tv reviewers while  nearly everyone can agree that beavis  and butthead is great plenty of older  fans remember how controversial the show  once was today most critics and tv  viewers understand the point to beavis  and butthead yes the characters are both  dumb as bags of rocks both of them are  obsessed with sex have juvenile senses  of humor and engage in all kinds of  destructive behavior everyone  understands that creator mike judge  doesn't endorse these shenanigans  instead the show is a satire one that  poked fun at adults perceptions of  generation xers who watched mtv however  at the time many critics completely  missed the point for just one example  the mclaughlin group spent an entire  segment bashing the show and complaining  that it represented the decline of  american television crude dumb ugly  thoughtless sexist self-destructive and  foolish the generational divide was also  a factor in 1993 a san diego union  tribune critic summed it up best by  writing i tried to like beavis and  butthead i really did in fact it  actually bothered me that i didn't like  them i always wanted to be a cool parent  i don't want to be part of another older  generation but i can't help it i really  really hate these guys strangely many of  these critics thought that mike judge  was just as dumb as the characters he  created as judge later put it viewers  really should have connected the dots  after all how could someone be capable  of producing a professional level piece  of animation and still be as dumb as  beavis and butthead appear to be still  given the overall reception plenty of  parents in 1993 thought that beavis and  butthead was too dangerous for tv  in october 1993 a five-year-old in  moraine ohio named austin messner  allegedly started a fire that resulted  in the death of his two-year-old sister  jessica his mother darcy burke then  claimed that her son had watched beavis  and butthead and that the show inspired  him to play with fire of the incident  the local fire chief harold ziegler told  the associated press the mother is  attributing the fact that he was  fascinated with fire to the beavis and  butthead segments where they are setting  things on fire when you take a child in  the formative years and you get these  cartoon characters saying it's fun to  play with fire this is going to stick in  that kid's mind and it's going to be  with him for a long time mtv didn't go  so far as to take beavis and butthead  off the air but the network did make  several adjustments in an attempt to  head off the criticism the network  decided to ban the characters from  saying the word fire removed four  episodes from the rerun schedule and  moved the show from 10 pm to 11 30 pm  hoping that only older viewers would be  watching however in a 2011 interview  with the spokesman review judge denied  that beavis and butthead had such an  influence on children saying first of  all i don't agree with any of that kind  of criticism and i don't take any  responsibility for any of it at all the  fire was obviously a very horrible sad  tragedy but it had nothing to do with  beavis and butthead years later austin  messner reportedly came forward and  clarified that he had never even seen  bevison butthead because his family  couldn't afford cable at the time the  controversy ultimately didn't stop  beavis and butthead from becoming the  cultural icon than it is today it would  go on to spawn the 1996 film beavis and  butthead do america a 2011 reboot on mtv  and the most recent feature-length  offering not bad for a show that many  initially condemned  [Music]

